  "gd_title": {
    "message": "Aubade"
  },
  "gd_h0": {
    "message": "Your new tab"
  },
  "gd_b0": {
    "message": "The time, the date, today's solar term. Every tab you open from now on is this page, so it had better be worth looking at."
  },
  "gd_h1": {
    "message": "The search box does more than search"
  },
  "gd_b1": {
    "message": "Type an address and you go there; type anything else and you search. Start with a single letter and a space to switch engine — g for Google, y for YouTube. Ctrl K opens the command palette from anywhere."
  },
  "gd_h2": {
    "message": "The row below is where you go often"
  },
  "gd_b2": {
    "message": "Hover a tile for two small buttons: one edits its address and name, one removes it. Drag a tile to reorder. Sixteen fit on a card."
  },
  "gd_next": {
    "message": "Next"
  },
  "gd_skip": {
    "message": "Skip"
  },
  "gd_done": {
    "message": "Start"
  },
  "gd_h3": {
    "message": "There's a second screen"
  },
  "gd_b3": {
    "message": "To-dos, notes, a pomodoro timer, the calendar, the weather, what's playing. Drag a card by its header, pull its corner to resize — this screen is yours to arrange."
  },
  "gd_h4": {
    "message": "Cards grow"
  },
  "gd_b4": {
    "message": "The calendar and the timer have an expand button that opens them full screen. Make the weather card big enough and it becomes live radar over your city."
  },
  "gd_h5": {
    "message": "Click the clock"
  },
  "gd_b5": {
    "message": "A full dial that turns: the twelve double-hours, the twenty-four solar terms, today's arc of daylight, the twenty-eight mansions in the corners. Leave it open and it breathes."
  },
  "gd_h6": {
    "message": "That gear, bottom right"
  },
  "gd_b6": {
    "message": "Whether the background is the hour's gradient, a flat colour, or your own photo; which cards appear; a twelve or twenty-four hour clock; which city the weather follows. Settings has four pages — general, look, cards, data — and the last one exports the lot to a file you can carry to another machine."
  },
